-- title:
--   Descended per-node block at one end, q=2
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q = 2$ (hypothesis `hq2`), $M'$ is a non-zero natural number, and $\ell_g$ is a prime with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$ (`hℓg`, `hℓg12`, `hℓgM'`). The level group is $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$, and `hH₁` fixes it as the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) (the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$) with the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/\ell_g)^\times$.
--
--   **Reduction data.** $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` with `hA : A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; `hqM'` asserts $q \nmid M'$. $W$ is a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`, and `hW` identifies it with the set `ssPlaces q M'` of supersingular places (rational affine geometric places whose value at the generator $j$ lies in `ssJSet q`), $s$ being a chosen member of $W$. The inclusion `hle` states `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`. $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`, and `hR₀` requires its residue map to be computed coefficientwise: for every Laurent series over $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element belongs to `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over the residue field of $A$, is the coefficientwise reduction.
--
--   **Constants.** $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$, $\pi_0 \in k_0$ with $\pi_0 \in A$ (`hπ`), and $A_0$ denotes the valuation subring of $k_0$ obtained by contracting $A$ along $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. The hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres` require $A_0$ to be a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal $(\pi_0)$, henselian, with algebraically closed residue field, and `hκ` requires every element of $A$ to be congruent, modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, to an element of $k_0 \cap A$.
--
--   **Auxiliary elements of the frame.** A prime $\ell$ with `hℓ`, `hℓ3` ($3 \le \ell$), `hℓq` ($\ell \ne q$), `hℓM'` ($\ell \nmid M'$); $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity (`hζ₀`); $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ (`hϖtA`) with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for a unit $u$ of $A$ (`hϖt`), and $\varpi_t' \in A_0$ equal to it (`hϖt'`); $\xi \in k_0$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity (`hξ`); an intermediate field $K_b$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$ with $K_b = \bot$ (`hKb`), a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ compatible with $A$ (`hAb`) and $\varpi_b \in A_b$ generating its maximal ideal (`hϖb`) and non-zero (`hϖb0`); the tameness hypothesis `htame` that $(\ell_g-1)/2$ is a unit of $A_0$.
--
--   **The rigid-level function field and the chart.** $K_\ell$ is an intermediate field of `LaurentSeries k₀` over $k_0$, with `hKℓ` identifying it with the base change to $k_0$ of the function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79); it carries an $A_0$-algebra structure compatible with $k_0$. The element $j_\ell \in K_\ell$ is non-zero and equals the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion $j_q$ (`hjℓ`). Write $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A₀ Kℓ jℓ`, the subalgebra of elements of $K_\ell$ integral over $A_0[j_\ell]$. The ideal $y \subset C$ is maximal (`hy`) and contains $\pi_0$ (`hϖy`); `hjK` asserts [`ModularCurve.jqNModC k₀ q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) $\in K_\ell$, `hjC` that it lies in $C$, and `ha₀y` that its difference from the constant $a_0 \in A_0$ lies in $y$. The hypothesis `hss` requires that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the image of `jChartFin` is a supersingular $j$-invariant, i.e. lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7). The hypothesis `hover` identifies $y$ as the point over $s$: for every $g$ in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-base change lies in `R₀.integers`, has non-negative order at every place at which $j_q$ does, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and whose image in $K_\ell$ lies in $C$, the difference of that image from any constant $c \in k_0 \cap A$ whose residue equals the value of the $R_0$-residue of $g$ at $s$ lies in $y$. The hypothesis `hOrbit` states that every maximal ideal $y'$ of $C$ containing $\pi_0$ with the same property is a translate of $y$: there exist $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and an automorphism $\tau$ of $K_\ell/k_0$ with `IsLevelAutAt k₀ q ξ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ Kℓ τ` — the condition that $\tau$ acts on ratios of modular forms of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ through the slash action of the matrix `conjElemN q γ⁻¹`, compared under embeddings of $k_0$ into $\mathbb{C}$ sending $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$ — such that $\tau$ preserves $C$ and carries $y$ to $y'$.
--
--   **The rigid model.** $B_t$ is an $A_0$-subalgebra of $K_\ell$ and $W_t$ a valuation subring of $K_\ell$ containing $B_t$ (`hBW`). The hypothesis `hS1` (thirteen clauses, summarised here) requires: $C \le B_t$ and $K_\ell$ is the fraction field of $B_t$; $B_t$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_0$; $B_t/\pi_0$ has Krull dimension at most one; $W_t$ meets $k_0$ in $A_0$, is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, contracts to $y$ on $C$, and is the localisation of $B_t$ at the complement of its maximal ideal; for every $\mathrm{GF}(q^2)$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A_0$ there is a surjection $\rho$ from $B_t$ onto the Drinfeld coordinate ring [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) of that residue field with kernel the contraction of the maximal ideal of $W_t$, compatible with $A_0$ and equivariant for level automorphisms through [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325), with a non-triviality clause on the scalar part and a companion automorphism realising the scalar alone; $B_t$ is stable under all level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$; every prime of $B_t$ containing $\pi_0$ is a level translate of the maximal ideal of $W_t$; and an element of $B_t$ all of whose level translates lie in the maximal ideal of $W_t$ is divisible by $\pi_0$.
--
--   **Cyclic data, crossing exponent, ends.** $n \ge 1$ divides $q+1$ (`hn1`, `hnq`) and equals `placeWidthChar q M' s` (`hn`); $\gamma_0 \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ (`hγ₀Γ`, `hγ₀Γ0`) with $\tau_0$ a level automorphism for $\gamma_0^{-1}$ (`hτ₀`) preserving $W_t$ (`hτ₀W`); $m \ge 1$ (`hm1`) with $\pi_0^m = \varpi_t'$ times a unit of $A_0$ (`hm`); $\zeta_c$ in the adic completion $\hat A_0$ of $A_0$ with $\zeta_c^n = 1$ (`hζc`) and $\zeta_c^k - 1$ a unit for $0 < k < n$ (`hζcprim`). A finite set `ends` of subrings of $K_\ell$ is given. The hypothesis `hR7` (eleven clauses, summarised here) requires: $\tau_0$ has exact order $n$ on $B_t$ and every level automorphism preserving $W_t$ agrees on $B_t$ with a power of $\tau_0$; `ends` has $q+1$ elements, is permuted transitively by the level automorphisms preserving $W_t$, each end is preserved by $\tau_0$, and distinct ends are separated by an element that is a non-unit in one and a unit in the other; there is a $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$-stable finite-type $A_0$-subalgebra contained in all ends and presenting each end as a localisation; a criterion for a level automorphism to preserve $W_t$; and, for each end $O$, that $O$ lies in $W_t$, is local and noetherian, contains $C$, meets $k_0$ in $A_0$, has constant residues, and admits a crossing presentation: an isomorphism $\iota$ of the adic completion of $O$ with the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` over $\hat A_0$ at $\hat\pi_0^{\,m}$ (the quotient of $\hat A_0[[X_0,X_1]]$ by $X_0X_1 - \hat\pi_0^{\,m}$) carrying constants to constants, with $c_xc_y = \pi_0^m u$, $\iota(c_x) = \gamma_U U$, $\iota(c_y) = \gamma_V V$, $c_y$ in and $c_x$ outside the maximal ideal of $W_t$, the reading $\iota(j_{q,N} - a_0) = w_V V^e$ with $e \ge 1$, the intertwining of $\tau_0$ with an automorphism $\theta_0$ satisfying $\theta_0(U) \equiv \zeta_c U$ and $\theta_0(V) \equiv \zeta_c' V$ modulo the square of the maximal ideal, and the existence of a branch valuation subring $W_x$ and of a level-stable finite-type subalgebra $B_x$ with the expected order, localisation and separation properties; finally a dichotomy: a valuation subring of $K_\ell$ meeting $k_0$ in $A_0$, containing $C$ and centred on $y$ either contains $B_t$ or dominates one of the ends. The hypotheses `hR9` and `hR10` provide escape elements of $B_t$: one detecting valuation subrings in which $j_\ell$ is non-integral and which omit some element, and one for each maximal ideal of $C$ over $\pi_0$ not in the level orbit of $y$.
--
--   **Descent data.** $G$ is the subgroup of $\mathrm{Aut}(K_\ell/k_0)$ generated by the level automorphisms attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ (`hG`), $K_0$ its fixed field (`hK₀`), $B_0$ the $G$-invariants of $B_t$ (`hB₀`), and $W_0'$ the contraction of $W_t$ to $K_0$ (`hW₀'`). A finite set `nodes` of subrings of $K_0$ is given, $\tilde O \in$ `ends` (`hÕ`), and $O$ is the subring of $K_0$ contracting $\tilde O$ (`hO`). The remaining hypotheses record the facts the descent needs: `hGfin` ($G$ finite), `hτ₀G`, `hGatt` (every element of $G$ is attached to some $\gamma$), `hτ₀n` ($\tau_0^n = \mathrm{id}$), `hHcyc` (an element of $G$ preserving $\tilde O$ is a power of $\tau_0$), `hInvFin` (for a $G$-stable finite-type subalgebra and its ring of invariants: noetherianity, module-finiteness, and finite generation of the contraction to $K_0$ over the constants), `hAdom`, `hAdvr`, `hAcompl`, `hπhat` ($\hat A_0$ is a complete discrete valuation domain with maximal ideal generated by the image of $\pi_0$), `hnunit` ($n$ is a unit of $\hat A_0$), `hmodelloc` and `hmodelcompl` (the crossing model at $\hat\pi_0^{\,m}$ is local and adically complete), `hsplit₁` and `hsplit₂` (existence of $G$-invariant elements separating $W_t$ from a branch ring, respectively witnessing a non-unit of $\tilde O$ outside the maximal ideal of $W_t$), `hN3wit` (descent of the coefficient-witness element $t$), `hN3laws` (descent of the reduction dictionary for level-$M'$ modular functions to $K_0$), `hN4frac` (descent of fraction presentations), `hjfix` ($G$ fixes `jqNModC k₀ q`), `hN5` (descent of the escape element), and `hIGSEP` (separation of the descended nodes).
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under these hypotheses the following holds. First, $O \subseteq W_0'$. Secondly, there are structures making $O$ a local noetherian ring, and for these:
--
--   (i) for $x \in k_0$, $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $K_0$ lies in $O$;
--
--   (ii) every $f \in O$ is congruent to a constant: there is $x \in k_0$ with $x \in A$ and image in $O$ such that $f - x$ is not a unit of $O$;
--
--   (iii) there exist a natural number $E_0 \ge 1$, a unit $v$ of $A_0$ (an element $v \in k_0$ with $v$ and $v^{-1}$ in $A$) with $\pi_0^{E_0} = \varpi_t^{\,\mathrm{pwc}} v$, where $\mathrm{pwc} =$ `placeWidthChar q M' s`, a proof that $\pi_0$ lies in $O$, elements $c_x, c_y \in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the adic completion of $O$ onto `UVCrossingModel` over $\hat A_0$ at $\hat\pi_0^{\,E_0}$, and units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ of that model, such that:
--
--   (1) $c_x c_y = \pi_0^{E_0} u$ in $O$;
--
--   (2) $\iota$ sends the image of each constant $x \in k_0 \cap A$ lying in $O$ to `UVCrossingModel.const` of its image in $\hat A_0$;
--
--   (3) $\iota(c_x) = \gamma_U \cdot U(\hat\pi_0^{\,E_0})$;
--
--   (4) $\iota(c_y) = \gamma_V \cdot V(\hat\pi_0^{\,E_0})$;
--
--   (5) $c_y$ lies in $W_0'$ and in its maximal ideal, while $c_x$, if it lies in $W_0'$, lies outside the maximal ideal;
--
--   (6) the element `jqNModC k₀ q` $- a_0$ lies in $K_0$ and in $O$, and there are $e \ge 1$ and a unit $w_V$ of the model with $\iota$ of this element equal to $w_V \cdot V(\hat\pi_0^{\,E_0})^e$;
--
--   (7) there is a valuation subring $W_x$ of $K_0$ such that $O \subseteq W_x$; for $x \in k_0$, $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ lies in $W_x$; $W_x$ is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $\pi_0$; there is $t \in W_x$ such that for every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ with all coefficients in $A$, if $p(t)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ then every coefficient of $p$ lies in it; $c_x$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ and $c_y$ outside it (in each case whenever the element lies in $W_x$); the reduction dictionary holds: for every $g$ in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-base change lies in `R₀.integers` and has non-negative order at every place where $j_q$ does, and whose image `coeffEmb k₀ g` lies in $K_\ell$, that image lies in $K_0$ and in $W_x$, lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ precisely when the $R_0$-residue of $g$ vanishes, and, if that residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image lies in $O$ and its difference from any constant $c \in k_0 \cap A$ whose residue equals the value of the residue of $g$ at $s$ is a non-unit of $O$; and finally every $O' \in$ `nodes` with $O' \ne O$ contains an element not in $W_x$;
--
--   (8) there is a subring $B_x$ of $K_0$ such that every $f \in B_x$ lies in $O$ and has image in $B_0$; for $f \in B_x$ and every place $P$ of $K_\ell$ over $k_0$ with $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(j_\ell)$ one has $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(f)$; $O$ is the localisation of $B_x$ in the sense that $f \in O$ if and only if $f h = g$ for some $g, h \in B_x$ with $h$ a unit of $O$ whenever it lies in $O$; $K_0$ is the fraction field of $B_x$, i.e. every $f \in K_0$ satisfies $fh = g$ with $g, h \in B_x$ and $h \ne 0$; there is a finite subset $T$ of $K_0$ with $B_x$ the subring generated by the constants $\{x \in k_0 : x \in A\}$ together with $T$; and there is $b \in B_x$ with the following escape property: for every valuation subring $V$ of $K_0$ meeting $k_0$ exactly in $A$, with the image of $\pi_0$ in the maximal ideal of $V$, and such that the image of $j_q$ lies in $K_0$ and in $V$ with no monic polynomial over $A_0$ evaluated at it lying in the maximal ideal of $V$, if some element of $O$ is not in $V$ then $b \notin V$.
--
--   This is the per-node block of the descent of the supersingular rigid model of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ to the fixed field $K_0 = K_\ell^G$, in the $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$ diamond frame at the prime $q = 2$: it transports the crossing presentation, branch valuation ring, reduction dictionary and escape elements from one end $\tilde O$ of the rigid model to the descended local ring $O = \tilde O \cap K_0$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.pernodeConclusion_traces_of_rigidChart_linkedScalars_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.pernodeConclusion_traces_of_rigidChart_linkedScalars_of_eq_two_of_dvd) in the construction of the semistable model at the supersingular points, which feeds the level-lowering step.
